📈 Model Diagnostics
Detailed analysis of model confidence and class-wise discrimination.


ROC Curves (One-vs-Rest)


Code
filtered_roc = {
  const data = transpose(roc_curves);
  // We match by the first run in the current filter for simplicity
  const run_name = filtered_data.length &gt; 0 ? filtered_data[0].full_run_name : "";
  return data.filter(d =&gt; d.full_run_name === run_name);
}

Plot.plot({
  grid: true,
  aspectRatio: 1,
  x: {label: "False Positive Rate (FPR)", domain: [0, 1]},
  y: {label: "True Positive Rate (TPR)", domain: [0, 1]},
  color: {legend: true},
  marks: [
    Plot.line([0, 1], {x: d =&gt; d, y: d =&gt; d, stroke: "#ccc", strokeDasharray: "4,4"}), // Random chance line
    Plot.line(filtered_roc, {
      x: "fpr", 
      y: "tpr", 
      stroke: "class",
      tip: true
    })
  ]
})


















Performance Summary
Analyze the class-wise separation. High TPR at low FPR indicates a high-fidelity classifier for that news category.
